# Copy this file to `.env` and fill it in. `.env` is ignored by git.

# Sign in with Google.
#
# 1. Go to https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials (any Google account).
# 2. Create a project if asked, then "Create credentials" → "OAuth client ID".
#    If it asks for a consent screen first, choose "External" and fill in the
#    app name and your email — nothing else is needed for sign-in.
# 3. Application type: "Web application".
# 4. Authorised JavaScript origins: add every address the studio is opened at,
#    exactly, e.g.  http://localhost:5173  (and your real domain when hosted).
#    No redirect URI is needed.
# 5. Paste the client ID below (it ends in .apps.googleusercontent.com) and
#    restart `npm run dev`.
#
# The client ID is not a secret — it is sent to every browser — so it is safe
# in a VITE_ variable. There is no client secret to add.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
